<title>UK: Labour warns Brit Airways over slots-paper.</title>
<headline>Labour warns Brit Airways over slots-paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>An incoming Labour government would resist any moves by British Airways Plc to switch domestic flights from London's Heathrow to Gatwick airport, just south of Britain's capital, the Financial Times reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The newspaper cited Labour's shadow transport secretary Andrew Smith as saying he was prepared to use powers under European Union regulations to protect Heathrow services because of their importance to the local economy.</p>
<p>British Airways has already announced plans to switch several services between Heathrow and the southwest of England to Gatwick.</p>
<p>Critics believe British Airways plans the switch to free Heathrow slots to increase services to the U.S., the Financial Times said.</p>
<p>British Airways is being criticised by rival airlines over its planned alliance with AMR Corp's American Airlines. Such a link-up would result in the two companies controlling more than 60 percent of the air traffic between Britain and the U.S.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
